        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXsBMfhVdujzpBgKNOtiq6peUrzwgDX1szygyHvvAecGzSmHoMS=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3",
        "rating": 2,
        "relative_time_description": "6 years ago",
        "text": "House built in 2000 by Habitations Menotec Inc. A second hole for the pump in the basement was covered with black sheathing. This led to a visit from voles and subsequent water damage in the basement. Mr. Ménard came to plug the hole. Following a Rénoclimat inspection in 2016, to my surprise, the bathroom vent was venting into the attic. Mold covered one entire side of the plywood, and the attic trusses needed replacing at my expense. Mr. Ménard came to repair it and install the vent in the soffit. I now have to get the work done by someone else since I still have a mold problem in the attic. I'm questioning his competence, but I'll stop there.",
